From b1d9d12ce292f0de05f18fc2598c056f4548d596 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xbox360 Blades <xbox360-blades@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:32:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 52/55] Input: PC-style keyboard and mouse, used together with
 a controller

The keyboard (keyboard_mode 1) gets PC-game defaults: W A S D left stick,
Space / Enter A, C / Backspace B, R / E X, Q / wheel Y, G / F bumpers,
right / left mouse button LT / RT, Shift and V / middle button stick
clicks, Esc Start, Tab Back, Home Guide, arrows D-pad. MOUSE1-3 and WHEEL
are binding tokens.

Mouse aim (mouse_aim, mouse_sensitivity, mouse_deadzone_offset,
mouse_invert_y): a click in the window captures the mouse (hidden, kept
in the window) and its speed becomes the right stick, past the games'
dead zone; F8 (mouse_release_key) or losing focus releases it.

InputSystem::GetState combines every device on a player's slot (buttons
together, each trigger / stick from whichever pushes it further), so a
controller no longer hides the keyboard and mouse. Esc no longer leaves
fullscreen while the keyboard is a controller (F11 does).

